# Two-port production proxy example (nginx)

Terminates TLS for both public entrances and forwards to the two Server
listeners. Replace hostnames, ports, and certificate paths with your own values.
The AGENT entrance must forward WebSocket upgrades.

```nginx
# Browser entrance
server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name terminal.example.com;
    ssl_certificate     /etc/letsencrypt/live/terminal.example.com/fullchain.pem;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/terminal.example.com/privkey.pem;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8080;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;

        # Browser terminal WebSocket
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
        proxy_read_timeout 3600s;
        proxy_buffering off;
    }
}

# Agent entrance (dedicated public port)
server {
    listen 8443 ssl;
    server_name terminal.example.com;
    ssl_certificate     /etc/letsencrypt/live/terminal.example.com/fullchain.pem;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/terminal.example.com/privkey.pem;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8443;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;

        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
        proxy_read_timeout 3600s;
        proxy_buffering off;
        client_max_body_size 4m;
    }
}
```

Notes:

- The two entrances use **different ports** (or different hostnames pointing at
  different listeners). Separate paths on one port do not satisfy the two-port
  requirement.
- The WEB listener itself may speak plain HTTP inside the trusted network; only
  the public entrance needs TLS. The AGENT listener can terminate TLS itself via
  `AGENT_TLS_CERT`/`AGENT_TLS_KEY`, in which case a TCP-stream proxy is sufficient.
- Set `WEB_ORIGIN=https://terminal.example.com` and
  `AGENT_ORIGIN=https://terminal.example.com:8443` on the Server.
